  "description": "Subject: Traffic Controller\u202f#42 \u2013 Status Summary (15\u202fJune\u202f2026, 08:30\u202f+02:00)\n\nAt cycle second\u202f120 the controller identified by domain UUID\u202f123e4567\u2011e89b\u201112d3\u2011a456\u2011426614174000 (unit\u202f42) was running program\u202f3. The current permission set consists of **read**, **write** and **execute**. Configured variables are\u202fmaxSpeed\u202f=\u202f80 (km/h) and\u202fmode\u202f=\u202fautomatic. Detector activity for this interval showed detector\u202f2 flanking at\u202f100\u202fms and again at\u202f900\u202fms, while detector\u202f4 (named\u202fA1) recorded a flank at\u202f700\u202fms. Signal changes were reported for two groups: group\u202f1 (labelled \u201cMain\u201d) switched to OCIT code\u202f5, and group\u202f2 switched to code\u202f2.\n\nA public\u2011transport telegram was received from detection point\u202f10 for line\u202f5. The telegram indicates course\u202f1, route\u202f2, priority\u202f1, vehicle length\u202f12\u202fm, manual direction\u202f0 and no schedule deviation (abw\u202f=\u202f0). The accompanying AMLI extension reports a calculated travel time of\u202f45\u202fseconds, a desired phase (UE) of\u202f3, green start\u202f120\u202fseconds and green end\u202f150\u202fseconds for the OV signal group, a running phase (PH) of\u202f2, no active modification flag, a relative node number\u202f7, the active signal plan\u202f4 and a time\u2011switch value of\u202f0."
